A||||3||pontiacs4me||weird electrical problem||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||03-03-2001||03:34 AM||||Ok, today I decided to ground the green and white wire on the electric fan relay.  Afterwards something weird happened, the front speakers started popping.  It sounded like they bottomed out all the way and did it about 7 times, then stopped.  Every time I start the car it does the same thing.  What gives?  Anyone had this problem before?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||03-03-2001||09:17 PM||||Now it gets even weirder.  Today the whole car shut down on me.  Turned out it was corrosion on the negative battery terminal.  After that was fixed the popping noise started whenever I change the position of the blower motor switch.  I am putting a new alternator on it tomorrow hopefully that will solve it.  It seems that it isnt up to all it can do.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||03-04-2001||04:47 PM||||Your problem could be loose connections on the braided ground strap between the engine block and the chassis (actually, the decklid hinge bolt on the passanger side).  This ground strap provides the ground connection between the alternator and EVERYTHING else.  I had to retighten the bolts on this strap several times in the last couple years.  The simptoms were very much as you described...loud popping sounds from speakers whenever any electrical load was turned on (i.e., brake lights, blower, headlights, etc.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||03-05-2001||04:33 PM||||Now that I think about it, I dont even have a braided ground strap.  One of the loop ends was broken off and I threw it away.  Ill get a new one and try that.  thanks alot<BR>||||reg||1
